1
00:00:00,230 --> 00:00:01,270
I'm begging you.

2
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:02,790
Can you let Anda go for now?

3
00:00:02,870 --> 00:00:04,520
I told you I didn't kill him.

4
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:06,360
How could I hurt the person I love most?

5
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:07,880
Where did you get these earbuds?

6
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:09,170
I bought them from an online shop.

7
00:00:09,290 --> 00:00:09,980
Is it this one?

8
00:00:10,330 --> 00:00:11,430
We've got stuff from...

9
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:13,010
Yeah, they're live right now.

10
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:14,930
The jacket the vendor is wearing...

11
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:16,840
I bought it for Anda.

12
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:18,200
Where did you get this jacket?

13
00:00:18,230 --> 00:00:19,470
From the dead man's car, right?

14
00:00:20,410 --> 00:00:24,850
Dad, who did you sell
the dead man's phone and laptop to?

15
00:00:24,930 --> 00:00:25,850
Those things...

16
00:00:25,870 --> 00:00:28,360
are with someone
we should stay far away from.

17
00:00:28,910 --> 00:00:30,890
Sir, please buy some cupcakes.

18
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:33,390
Have something first,
then I'll buy your cupcakes.

19
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:39,110
You deserve a reward
when you do something good.

20
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:41,220
Do you want anything?

21
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:42,370
I'll get it for you.

22
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:44,670
I can buy it myself.

23
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:46,560
I'm sure there's something

24
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:48,000
that you really want,

25
00:00:48,370 --> 00:00:50,010
but money can't buy.

26
00:00:50,740 --> 00:00:53,800
I don't care whether or not you like Jin.

27
00:00:53,830 --> 00:00:55,160
He doesn't belong to anyone yet,

28
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:57,090
so let's compete to win him over.

29
00:00:57,230 --> 00:00:58,030
Deal?

30
00:01:05,330 --> 00:01:06,650
So...

31
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:10,010
do you still have practice today?

32
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:12,940
I'll probably practice for a bit more.

33
00:01:14,450 --> 00:01:16,520
Oh, how many hours
have you practiced already?

34
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:20,160
I think it'll be over soon.

35
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:21,980
So, about another hour?

36
00:01:22,820 --> 00:01:23,550
Ouch...

37
00:01:23,690 --> 00:01:27,310
Do you know what the concept
for our college photo shoot is?

38
00:01:27,789 --> 00:01:28,830
I don't know.

39
00:01:29,030 --> 00:01:30,050
Give me a second, I...

40
00:01:30,180 --> 00:01:31,580
I know it, though.

41
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:34,720
I'd better not tell you yet.
It'll be a surprise.

42
00:01:34,750 --> 00:01:37,820
The student council said that
it's perfect that it's you and me.

43
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:39,710
They said our chemistry is great.

44
00:01:39,810 --> 00:01:40,960
They're exaggerating.

45
00:01:42,789 --> 00:01:43,970
What did I do to deserve this?

46
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:45,610
Why do I have to watch them get all lovey-dovey?

47
00:01:48,270 --> 00:01:51,460
How do you feel about being paired with me?

48
00:01:51,490 --> 00:01:53,060
Well, it's good.

49
00:01:54,130 --> 00:01:56,490
Sorry, I have to go.

50
00:01:56,509 --> 00:01:57,100
Hey.

51
00:01:57,130 --> 00:01:59,110
Risa...

52
00:02:00,090 --> 00:02:01,190
What are you doing here?

53
00:02:01,470 --> 00:02:03,400
Oh, I'm here to see Jin.

54
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:04,930
Here?

55
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:05,850
Yeah.

56
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:15,630
[The depicted characters, behaviors, locations,
organizations, professions, and events]

57
00:02:15,650 --> 00:02:17,390
[are fictional and created
for entertainment purposes only.]

58
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:19,930
[It is not intended to endorse or promote
any of the actions or behavior depicted.]

59
00:02:19,950 --> 00:02:21,230
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

60
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:40,130
♫I used to wonder what we were,♫

61
00:02:40,350 --> 00:02:46,230
♫I thought love needed something clearer,♫

62
00:02:46,950 --> 00:02:52,250
♫Took me time to learn what really matters♫

63
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:58,940
♫Love has no rules, whatever comes after♫

64
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:05,690
♫As long as I know what my heart wants to find,♫

65
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:08,730
♫As long as you're standing by my side,♫

66
00:03:08,750 --> 00:03:11,980
♫With you, the only one I'd choose every time,♫

67
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,760
♫I don't need a reason, as long as you're mine♫

68
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:19,170
♫As long as you hold my hand,♫

69
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,900
♫As long as next to me is where you stand,♫

70
00:03:21,930 --> 00:03:25,350
♫You're the one I'll always try to understand,♫

71
00:03:25,380 --> 00:03:29,110
♫No matter how hard the road may be,♫

72
00:03:29,570 --> 00:03:32,300
♫Just hold my hand, and we'll be free♫

73
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:35,829
♫As long as you're here with me♫

74
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:46,760
Can we talk?

75
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:48,160
About what?

76
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:50,700
About us.

77
00:03:53,410 --> 00:03:55,070
I don't have any feelings for Risa.

78
00:03:56,470 --> 00:03:57,920
Whatever you think has nothing to do with me.

79
00:03:58,579 --> 00:04:00,280
We're just pretending to flirt, remember?

80
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:01,870
It's not like we're actually flirting.

81
00:04:04,570 --> 00:04:06,250
Does it look like I'm pretending?

82
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:08,780
I like you.

83
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:10,650
Can't you tell?

84
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:16,040
Dork.

85
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:28,220
I like you.

86
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:30,000
Can't you tell?

87
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:31,630
Dork.

88
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:32,920
Dork.

89
00:05:06,910 --> 00:05:10,520
[Tell me when you're done with the exam.
I'll come to your faculty.]

90
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:11,200
[Jinna: Tell me when you're done with the exam.
I'll come to your faculty.]

91
00:05:18,660 --> 00:05:19,930
I've looked all over the mall.

92
00:05:20,140 --> 00:05:20,980
Didn't find anything.

93
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,490
Right, they might've been smuggled
to the border now.

94
00:05:26,210 --> 00:05:27,190
It's possible.

95
00:05:28,250 --> 00:05:29,290
But I hope...

96
00:05:30,350 --> 00:05:32,110
we'll find either Anda's laptop or phone.

97
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:37,140
But that security guard was really suspicious.

98
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:41,750
We just asked where he sold it,
but why couldn't he tell us?

99
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,159
Yeah.

100
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:45,640
What do you think we'll find
on Anda's phone?

101
00:05:47,730 --> 00:05:48,650
I don't know.

102
00:05:49,350 --> 00:05:50,300
But I think...

103
00:05:51,290 --> 00:05:54,900
he definitely had things
he didn't tell anyone, not even us.

104
00:06:00,990 --> 00:06:01,730
I'd better go.

105
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:03,910
What? Where are you going now?

106
00:06:04,340 --> 00:06:05,270
To pick up Podduang.

107
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:08,880
Yeah, guess you don't want us anymore.
We're strays now, huh?

108
00:06:09,750 --> 00:06:11,430
You have always been.

109
00:06:11,450 --> 00:06:13,260
Wow, woof-woof.

110
00:06:14,930 --> 00:06:16,310
Tod, paw.

111
00:06:16,950 --> 00:06:18,610
That's complete nonsense.

112
00:06:23,670 --> 00:06:25,480
Why the long face? Cheer up, man.

113
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:27,070
- I'm fine.
- After that exam...

114
00:06:29,340 --> 00:06:30,310
You're going to fail.

115
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:34,060
- What? You said I'm failing?
- You definitely are.

116
00:06:34,090 --> 00:06:35,890
Before you fail, I might fall.

117
00:06:36,220 --> 00:06:37,159
Come here.

118
00:06:37,190 --> 00:06:38,580
I'll teach you a lesson.

119
00:06:50,510 --> 00:06:51,370
Jin?

120
00:06:52,470 --> 00:06:53,240
Jin.

121
00:06:54,190 --> 00:06:55,300
See you, Dunk.

122
00:06:56,300 --> 00:06:57,080
Jin!

123
00:06:58,700 --> 00:06:59,470
Jin!

124
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:02,130
Hey.

125
00:07:02,970 --> 00:07:04,080
I'm tired.

126
00:07:04,650 --> 00:07:05,450
Jin.

127
00:07:06,940 --> 00:07:07,730
Jin!

128
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:14,260
What's wrong with you?

129
00:07:14,290 --> 00:07:15,040
Nothing.

130
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:16,740
Don't act like this with me.

131
00:07:17,180 --> 00:07:18,750
If you're mad about something, tell me.

132
00:07:18,870 --> 00:07:19,920
So I'll know and apologize.

133
00:07:21,490 --> 00:07:22,760
Are you sure you will?

134
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:25,120
Well, tell me first.

135
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:27,950
Do you still like him?

136
00:07:27,980 --> 00:07:29,020
Like who?

137
00:07:29,670 --> 00:07:30,630
Your best friend.

138
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:32,690
You mean Dunk?

139
00:07:33,060 --> 00:07:34,380
I've been over him for ages.

140
00:07:34,470 --> 00:07:36,430
Dunk and Bumm are basically my parents now.

141
00:07:37,780 --> 00:07:39,120
Are you sure you're over him?

142
00:07:39,810 --> 00:07:40,510
I am.

143
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:42,400
I even find his face funny.

144
00:07:42,890 --> 00:07:44,880
So you're mad just because of this?

145
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:45,940
That's nonsense.

146
00:07:46,270 --> 00:07:47,159
Well, you...

147
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:48,170
What?

148
00:07:48,540 --> 00:07:49,920
You were so touchy-feely with him.

149
00:07:50,150 --> 00:07:51,810
I've always been like this.

150
00:07:57,350 --> 00:07:58,060
Let go of me.

151
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:01,540
I understand,

152
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:03,730
but you're with me now.

153
00:08:03,870 --> 00:08:05,310
How can you be like that with others?

154
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:09,450
If you want to be touchy-feely,

155
00:08:09,470 --> 00:08:11,070
just do it with me.

156
00:08:11,590 --> 00:08:12,450
Okay?

157
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:14,840
Jin.

158
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:16,860
I'm serious, Podduang.

159
00:08:19,710 --> 00:08:21,110
Should we take this more seriously?

160
00:08:22,140 --> 00:08:23,750
I really like you.

161
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,430
I was so damn jealous.

162
00:08:25,870 --> 00:08:27,180
I'm crazy about you.

163
00:08:31,430 --> 00:08:32,340
Why so quiet?

164
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:34,860
You're blushing, aren't you?

165
00:08:35,309 --> 00:08:37,549
Who wouldn't?
There are so many people around.

166
00:08:41,809 --> 00:08:43,010
No one is looking.

167
00:08:44,340 --> 00:08:45,650
Fine, you can let go now.

168
00:08:45,880 --> 00:08:47,120
You still haven't answered me.

169
00:08:47,150 --> 00:08:48,260
Answer what?

170
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:49,930
Hey, I asked you a question.

171
00:08:51,780 --> 00:08:52,940
I already told you that...

172
00:08:53,610 --> 00:08:54,860
there's nothing between me and Dunk.

173
00:08:54,890 --> 00:08:56,280
I don't have feelings for him anymore.

174
00:08:56,310 --> 00:08:57,650
Not that question.

175
00:08:58,660 --> 00:09:00,240
What question, then?

176
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:02,010
Let go.

177
00:09:02,690 --> 00:09:04,930
- I told you to let go.
- I asked if we should take this more seriously.

178
00:09:05,930 --> 00:09:07,320
If you don't answer, I won't let go.

179
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:13,760
Fine, let's do it then.

180
00:09:16,310 --> 00:09:17,560
Everyone's looking.

181
00:09:18,410 --> 00:09:19,270
Just look at me.

182
00:09:20,410 --> 00:09:21,650
- Let me go.
- What?

183
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:42,240
Is this your aunt's house?

184
00:09:43,410 --> 00:09:44,880
She's the lady I'm renting a house from.

185
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:46,110
I'm close to her.

186
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:49,920
You're here?

187
00:09:50,260 --> 00:09:51,300
Let's eat.

188
00:09:52,230 --> 00:09:55,030
I missed you so much.
Give me a hug.

189
00:09:55,270 --> 00:09:56,000
Alright.

190
00:09:59,390 --> 00:10:00,920
You're Podduang, right?

191
00:10:01,290 --> 00:10:03,260
Jin mentioned you'd be coming along.

192
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:07,040
Yes. Hello, Auntie Amphon.

193
00:10:07,060 --> 00:10:08,360
No need to be formal.

194
00:10:09,310 --> 00:10:12,100
You must be tired.
Let me go get the soup first.

195
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:14,620
Auntie, you don't have to.

196
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:15,840
I'll handle it myself.

197
00:10:22,190 --> 00:10:25,030
That's just how Jin is.
He's more about actions than words.

198
00:10:25,060 --> 00:10:25,920
Let's have a seat.

199
00:10:25,940 --> 00:10:26,830
You must be tired.

200
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:28,020
Come on, dear.

201
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:29,290
Please.

202
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:36,110
How have you been?

203
00:10:36,220 --> 00:10:38,590
Jin didn't force you to come, did he?

204
00:10:39,630 --> 00:10:41,420
You seem like...

205
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,160
the type who gets talked into things easily.

206
00:10:45,870 --> 00:10:48,990
He didn't force me.
He actually asked me to come.

207
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:52,660
He told me he often has dinner with you.

208
00:10:52,680 --> 00:10:53,800
That's right.

209
00:10:54,250 --> 00:10:57,020
He comes here pretty often,
so I won't get lonely.

210
00:11:07,630 --> 00:11:09,530
This is Phera, my son.

211
00:11:09,860 --> 00:11:12,050
And this is his family.

212
00:11:16,910 --> 00:11:18,760
Your granddaughter is so cute.

213
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:20,700
How old is she?

214
00:11:22,810 --> 00:11:24,820
Didn't Jin tell you?

215
00:11:27,020 --> 00:11:28,150
About what?

216
00:11:32,340 --> 00:11:33,560
Last year,

217
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:36,510
Phera and his family...

218
00:11:37,990 --> 00:11:41,460
were in an accident and passed away.

219
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:42,960
I lost them all.

220
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:49,720
I'm sorry for your loss.

221
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:53,100
I'm sorry for asking about them.

222
00:11:53,640 --> 00:11:54,800
It's okay.

223
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:58,840
It's nice that Jin and his friends
come to keep me company.

224
00:12:01,460 --> 00:12:04,320
If it weren't for these kids, I don't know...

225
00:12:05,390 --> 00:12:08,610
how I'd go on.

226
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:13,350
Jin has a sixth sense.

227
00:12:13,370 --> 00:12:16,800
He heard someone calling for help,
so he went in to help.

228
00:12:17,630 --> 00:12:19,020
He ended up getting injured

229
00:12:19,530 --> 00:12:22,490
and had to stop playing sports for a year
because of that incident.

230
00:12:33,970 --> 00:12:35,620
That day...

231
00:12:36,870 --> 00:12:38,870
I couldn't save her son,

232
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:40,920
so I've been feeling guilty.

233
00:12:40,950 --> 00:12:44,110
I've got some sweet pomelo, guys.

234
00:12:46,750 --> 00:12:47,630
Thanks, Auntie.

235
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:52,150
Jin, when you leave,

236
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:53,930
make sure to lock the door.

237
00:12:54,130 --> 00:12:56,290
But if you want to stay overnight,
that's fine, too.

238
00:12:56,310 --> 00:12:59,000
I've already prepared
the pillows and blankets for you.

239
00:12:59,090 --> 00:13:00,790
Got it, Auntie.

240
00:13:00,890 --> 00:13:02,260
I'm going to bed now.

241
00:13:02,810 --> 00:13:03,460
Goodbye.

242
00:13:03,490 --> 00:13:04,630
- Goodbye.
- Have a good night.

243
00:13:04,650 --> 00:13:06,010
Alright, I will.

244
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:15,230
You seem really close to her.

245
00:13:16,460 --> 00:13:17,800
She's all alone,

246
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:19,980
so I come to see her often.

247
00:13:21,060 --> 00:13:24,540
You always carry everyone
on your back, don't you?

248
00:13:25,830 --> 00:13:26,760
What do you mean?

249
00:13:28,260 --> 00:13:30,530
I mean, everything.

250
00:13:32,450 --> 00:13:33,710
You seem to...

251
00:13:34,910 --> 00:13:36,240
love taking care of others

252
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:37,800
and doing things for them.

253
00:13:39,070 --> 00:13:40,370
To the point where you...

254
00:13:42,740 --> 00:13:44,980
put yourself last.

255
00:13:48,730 --> 00:13:50,200
You can be weak sometimes, Jin.

256
00:14:07,890 --> 00:14:09,250
For those who matter,

257
00:14:10,170 --> 00:14:11,380
I can do anything.

258
00:14:17,670 --> 00:14:19,220
I can do anything for you, too.

259
00:14:21,740 --> 00:14:22,710
I know.

260
00:14:25,540 --> 00:14:27,330
But could you not overexert yourself?

261
00:14:29,790 --> 00:14:30,990
I get it,

262
00:14:31,710 --> 00:14:32,480
but...

263
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:35,710
I'll find out what happened to Anda first.

264
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:47,930
Why is it so complicated and mysterious?

265
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:50,680
There are only questions without answers.

266
00:14:52,110 --> 00:14:55,610
It'd be great if the mysterious earbuds
could answer everything we want to know.

267
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:02,480
By the way...

268
00:15:06,590 --> 00:15:10,070
Where did that vendor in the livestream
get the earbuds from?

269
00:15:22,050 --> 00:15:24,090
Are you sure you got them
from the security guard?

270
00:15:24,620 --> 00:15:25,940
I told you already.

271
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:28,270
That guard actually sold them to me.

272
00:15:28,710 --> 00:15:30,620
He always has things to sell me,

273
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:33,220
so I put them in boxes and resold them.

274
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:35,250
I'll talk to him myself.

275
00:15:35,630 --> 00:15:36,460
Bye.

276
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:41,890
So, the earbuds Dunk bought from that page...

277
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:46,510
Were they really from this security guard?

278
00:15:47,710 --> 00:15:49,940
Yes, that's what the vendor said.

279
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:52,300
Just the earbuds, though.
No laptop or phone.

280
00:15:52,780 --> 00:15:55,220
That means both Anda's jacket...

281
00:15:56,060 --> 00:15:57,510
and earbuds...

282
00:15:58,430 --> 00:16:00,790
were sold to that page by this security guard.

283
00:16:01,620 --> 00:16:02,480
That is why

284
00:16:03,180 --> 00:16:04,770
I'm here to ask him.

285
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:17,570
Why are you here again?

286
00:16:18,950 --> 00:16:20,810
What else did you take from Anda's car

287
00:16:20,870 --> 00:16:22,020
besides the jacket?

288
00:16:24,860 --> 00:16:25,840
These earbuds, too?

289
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:36,620
I thought they might be worth something,

290
00:16:36,650 --> 00:16:38,120
so I took them, too.

291
00:16:38,380 --> 00:16:41,000
But that kid only gave me a few coins.

292
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:43,200
I didn't get much at all.

293
00:16:44,740 --> 00:16:46,350
They really belonged to Anda.

294
00:17:27,010 --> 00:17:28,730
Who did this to you, Anda?

295
00:17:32,010 --> 00:17:33,640
Who did this to you?

296
00:17:43,650 --> 00:17:44,590
Let's go.

297
00:18:05,430 --> 00:18:06,720
Are you okay?

298
00:18:11,940 --> 00:18:12,920
Jin.

299
00:18:14,430 --> 00:18:15,150
Yeah.

300
00:18:21,150 --> 00:18:23,320
Wait, that car looks familiar.

301
00:18:37,770 --> 00:18:38,790
It's Amp.

302
00:18:40,980 --> 00:18:42,480
I'm not seeing things, am I?

303
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:45,810
Amp?

304
00:18:46,810 --> 00:18:47,940
Your next-door neighbor?

305
00:18:50,250 --> 00:18:51,590
What now? What?

306
00:18:53,740 --> 00:18:54,880
How do they know each other?

307
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:57,580
- I don't know.
- Take it.

308
00:18:59,620 --> 00:19:00,980
I think it looks suspicious.

309
00:19:26,570 --> 00:19:27,730
Are you sure?

310
00:19:28,390 --> 00:19:30,220
Won't it look like we're being nosy?

311
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:32,360
Trust me, Podduang.

312
00:19:32,550 --> 00:19:34,120
If something feels off,

313
00:19:34,140 --> 00:19:35,540
we shouldn't ignore it.

314
00:19:35,830 --> 00:19:36,820
But Amp?

315
00:19:37,430 --> 00:19:38,410
What does she have to do with this?

316
00:19:39,040 --> 00:19:40,380
We'll find out soon enough.

317
00:19:49,860 --> 00:19:51,240
Is something wrong, Podduang?

318
00:19:52,710 --> 00:19:55,820
Oh, I just haven't seen you around much lately,

319
00:19:56,290 --> 00:19:58,420
so I thought I'd check in on you.

320
00:19:58,440 --> 00:19:59,840
Are you doing okay?

321
00:20:00,670 --> 00:20:04,400
Yeah, I'm fine. I was just sleeping.

322
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:06,100
I've been working from home.

323
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,360
Are you with someone, Amp?

324
00:20:10,530 --> 00:20:11,430
Jin.

325
00:20:14,060 --> 00:20:16,020
If that's all, I'll talk to you later.

326
00:20:18,670 --> 00:20:19,750
If you need anything...

327
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:22,330
you can find Podduang next door.

328
00:20:27,260 --> 00:20:28,660
How could you ask her that?

329
00:20:28,940 --> 00:20:30,120
It's personal.

330
00:20:30,210 --> 00:20:31,960
Couldn't you tell something was off?

331
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:33,670
She looked like she'd been hurt.

332
00:20:39,340 --> 00:20:40,600
Aren't you tired?

333
00:20:40,940 --> 00:20:42,110
Go home and get some sleep.

334
00:20:43,650 --> 00:20:46,050
No, I want to be with you.

335
00:20:47,610 --> 00:20:48,800
Come on.

336
00:20:49,100 --> 00:20:50,290
It's piping hot.

337
00:20:52,460 --> 00:20:53,370
Want some?

338
00:20:54,030 --> 00:20:55,130
- Want it?
- Sure.

339
00:20:56,590 --> 00:20:58,010
Jin, have you seen this?

340
00:20:58,540 --> 00:21:00,080
The lead actor is so handsome.

341
00:21:00,740 --> 00:21:01,730
I haven't.

342
00:21:01,910 --> 00:21:02,720
Let's watch it.

343
00:21:04,080 --> 00:21:04,760
Okay.

344
00:21:05,410 --> 00:21:07,570
You're so nice, unlike my brother.

345
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:10,530
He never watches anything with me.

346
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:12,250
And lately,

347
00:21:12,670 --> 00:21:14,200
he's been looking stressed every day.

348
00:21:14,500 --> 00:21:15,450
Don't know what's wrong with him.

349
00:21:15,470 --> 00:21:16,840
Seeing you makes me sad.

350
00:21:16,980 --> 00:21:18,850
Relax, come on.

351
00:21:36,110 --> 00:21:37,220
What's wrong, Podduang?

352
00:21:37,830 --> 00:21:38,780
Nothing.

353
00:21:52,140 --> 00:21:52,900
Satang.

354
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:55,590
What are you doing?
You're making a mess.

355
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:58,210
I'm cleaning it up. Stop complaining.

356
00:22:16,410 --> 00:22:17,700
Wait, there's more?

357
00:22:21,630 --> 00:22:22,640
- Satang.
- Yes?

358
00:22:22,660 --> 00:22:23,770
Over there, too.

359
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:26,180
Whoa...

360
00:22:26,620 --> 00:22:27,950
♫Is missing you what love feels like?♫

361
00:22:27,980 --> 00:22:29,220
♫You're always on my mind,♫

362
00:22:29,240 --> 00:22:31,580
♫Whatever I do,
I think of you all day and night,♫

363
00:22:31,610 --> 00:22:34,290
♫I guess this is what love feels like♫

364
00:22:34,310 --> 00:22:35,530
♫Will it break my heart if I say it tonight?♫

365
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:36,830
♫But I can't keep it inside♫

366
00:22:36,860 --> 00:22:39,330
♫I thought I was just lonely, nothing more,♫

367
00:22:39,350 --> 00:22:41,680
♫Then you came so casually,
like you'd done it before,♫

368
00:22:41,710 --> 00:22:44,460
♫You're simply being yourself,
yet somehow I fall,♫

369
00:22:44,490 --> 00:22:47,440
♫So, wanna give it a try and be my all?♫

370
00:22:48,220 --> 00:22:53,250
♫I'm caught off guard, I don't know what to do,♫

371
00:22:53,280 --> 00:22:58,260
♫So let me just tell you how much I love you♫

372
00:23:01,790 --> 00:23:03,590
Why are you going that way?

373
00:23:04,340 --> 00:23:06,790
Come on, it's just a few minutes.
You always take shortcuts.

374
00:23:06,940 --> 00:23:09,260
But this way is faster.

375
00:23:09,730 --> 00:23:12,410
You'll just hit small alleys,
and it'll take even longer.

376
00:23:13,700 --> 00:23:15,990
If we get there early,
we'll have more time.

377
00:23:16,250 --> 00:23:18,400
No, let's go this way.

378
00:23:18,490 --> 00:23:19,280
Dunk,

379
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:21,040
let's go this way.

380
00:23:23,820 --> 00:23:24,990
Bumm, hold this for me.

381
00:23:25,590 --> 00:23:26,460
Sure thing.

382
00:23:27,940 --> 00:23:29,330
Keep going straight.

383
00:23:33,650 --> 00:23:36,080
Come on, let's take this way.

384
00:23:40,070 --> 00:23:41,960
Jin is kinda fussy, isn't he?

385
00:23:42,690 --> 00:23:43,800
Don't say that.

386
00:23:44,380 --> 00:23:47,270
He just wants to take care of Podduang.

387
00:23:54,970 --> 00:23:58,290
Jin may seem calm and solid like a rock,

388
00:23:58,320 --> 00:24:00,430
but he seems to like you a lot, Podduang.

389
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:04,230
See, Dunk's been observing him all along.

390
00:24:04,250 --> 00:24:05,770
We totally ship you guys.

391
00:24:07,930 --> 00:24:10,200
You guys are so nosy.

392
00:24:11,220 --> 00:24:15,400
Well, of course.
People's business is mine, too.

393
00:24:19,510 --> 00:24:22,370
By the way, what are Art and Tod like?

394
00:24:22,780 --> 00:24:25,250
I feel like they're a bit eccentric, maybe?

395
00:24:26,620 --> 00:24:27,930
You'll find out when you get to know them.

396
00:24:27,960 --> 00:24:29,600
That's why I asked you guys to come along.

397
00:24:29,970 --> 00:24:32,090
Jin said he wanted us all to get close.

398
00:24:32,310 --> 00:24:33,420
No.

399
00:24:34,650 --> 00:24:37,070
Jin is so smooth.

400
00:24:57,170 --> 00:24:59,340
Sit in a better position if you're gonna sleep.

401
00:24:59,370 --> 00:25:01,200
You're gonna hurt your neck
sleeping like that.

402
00:25:05,050 --> 00:25:07,840
"You're gonna hurt your neck
sleeping like that."

403
00:25:08,670 --> 00:25:09,800
Aw.

404
00:25:10,310 --> 00:25:12,850
You two are seriously too much.

405
00:25:13,520 --> 00:25:16,560
Your voice is so soft when you talk to Podduang.

406
00:25:17,530 --> 00:25:18,630
I'm using my normal voice.

407
00:25:18,810 --> 00:25:21,840
Look at that. Talk about double standards.

408
00:25:21,860 --> 00:25:22,630
Soft...

409
00:25:23,800 --> 00:25:27,760
Come on, Tod, we're just his best friends.

410
00:25:28,650 --> 00:25:29,660
You know who he is?

411
00:25:31,130 --> 00:25:33,790
His sweetheart.

412
00:25:37,250 --> 00:25:39,590
Dunk, I'll drive on the way back.

413
00:25:40,760 --> 00:25:41,560
Jeez.

414
00:25:42,820 --> 00:25:44,340
Don't pretend to be shy.

415
00:25:44,540 --> 00:25:45,610
I know.

416
00:25:46,280 --> 00:25:48,500
On the way back,
you'll have someone sitting next to you.

417
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:49,910
Who?

418
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:51,160
Who could it be?

419
00:25:52,800 --> 00:25:54,920
It'll be my sweetheart next to me.
You happy now?

420
00:25:55,290 --> 00:25:56,770
- Whoa.
- Whoa.

421
00:25:56,830 --> 00:25:58,600
- "Sweetheart"?
- "Sweetheart"?

422
00:25:59,900 --> 00:26:01,850
Whoa.

423
00:26:02,900 --> 00:26:04,520
Don't try to run away from us.

424
00:26:04,670 --> 00:26:07,320
We're like wandering spirits,
following you everywhere.

425
00:26:07,340 --> 00:26:09,490
I'll have Dunk drop both of you right here

426
00:26:09,520 --> 00:26:10,740
if you don't shut your mouths.

427
00:26:24,300 --> 00:26:25,190
Move it.

428
00:26:29,740 --> 00:26:30,780
Hurry.

429
00:26:30,810 --> 00:26:33,210
Art, it's so cool in here.

430
00:26:33,240 --> 00:26:34,440
Damn, an arcade.

431
00:26:37,790 --> 00:26:39,770
This is such a classic.

432
00:26:41,230 --> 00:26:43,820
Damn, this house is huge, though.

433
00:26:44,030 --> 00:26:45,120
Who booked this?

434
00:26:45,540 --> 00:26:47,230
I did. I got it cheap, too.

435
00:26:47,440 --> 00:26:48,240
Impressive, huh?

436
00:26:49,010 --> 00:26:51,940
Whoa, you're the best.

437
00:26:52,590 --> 00:26:55,140
You're not only pretty but also smart.

438
00:26:56,620 --> 00:26:59,020
Her boyfriend is sitting right there, man.

439
00:26:59,080 --> 00:27:00,890
Jeez, you idiot.

440
00:27:00,920 --> 00:27:02,100
I was just complimenting her.

441
00:27:02,170 --> 00:27:04,290
It doesn't mean I like everyone I compliment.

442
00:27:04,480 --> 00:27:05,520
Look at Jin.

443
00:27:05,750 --> 00:27:06,920
I say he's handsome every day.

444
00:27:06,940 --> 00:27:08,000
As if I like him that much.

445
00:27:09,930 --> 00:27:12,110
So, how are we splitting the bedrooms?

446
00:27:12,390 --> 00:27:14,120
There are three rooms,
so it's perfect, right?

447
00:27:14,330 --> 00:27:17,020
Dunk and I will share one.
What about you guys?

448
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:19,490
Art and I will share one

449
00:27:19,630 --> 00:27:21,440
since we're roommates anyway.

450
00:27:22,650 --> 00:27:23,360
And...

451
00:27:24,660 --> 00:27:25,880
I...

452
00:27:26,090 --> 00:27:27,300
I prefer to sleep alone.

453
00:27:27,810 --> 00:27:29,350
I'll just sleep on the couch.

454
00:27:29,550 --> 00:27:31,680
Wait, why would you do that?

455
00:27:31,710 --> 00:27:33,020
You can just share a room with Jin.

456
00:27:34,220 --> 00:27:35,100
I'm good.

457
00:27:35,400 --> 00:27:36,890
I'm worried I won't be able to sleep.

458
00:27:37,880 --> 00:27:39,970
You can put your stuff in the room first.

459
00:27:40,280 --> 00:27:41,380
I'll sleep out here.

460
00:27:41,400 --> 00:27:44,080
I'll sleep on the couch.

461
00:27:44,240 --> 00:27:45,830
Just put your stuff in the room.

462
00:27:46,050 --> 00:27:48,890
- Whoa.
- Whoa.

463
00:27:49,300 --> 00:27:50,820
We're going to pick our room first.

464
00:27:50,880 --> 00:27:52,040
See you, guys.

465
00:27:54,100 --> 00:27:57,450
I'll put your stuff inside for you.

466
00:27:57,470 --> 00:27:59,010
It's okay. I'll do it myself.

467
00:27:59,320 --> 00:28:01,560
- It's okay. Let me help.
- It's okay.

468
00:28:01,580 --> 00:28:03,160
I can do it myself.

469
00:28:20,710 --> 00:28:21,710
What's everyone doing outside?

470
00:28:22,560 --> 00:28:24,510
Art and Tod are heading to the beach.

471
00:28:25,560 --> 00:28:27,850
Yeah, go ahead. It's still hot outside.

472
00:28:28,310 --> 00:28:29,640
I'll be there when it's cooler.

473
00:28:31,980 --> 00:28:33,620
You haven't slept with Jin yet, have you?

474
00:28:34,010 --> 00:28:35,400
What kind of question is that?

475
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:37,360
Come on, don't play innocent.

476
00:28:37,520 --> 00:28:38,890
It's natural.

477
00:28:39,800 --> 00:28:40,910
We haven't done anything yet.

478
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:43,210
We're not even dating yet.

479
00:28:44,240 --> 00:28:45,320
I knew it.

480
00:28:45,620 --> 00:28:47,040
Why are you so awkward around him?

481
00:28:47,300 --> 00:28:48,920
Why are you so shy?

482
00:28:49,930 --> 00:28:52,110
What do you mean? I'm not shy.

483
00:28:52,500 --> 00:28:53,680
You're not?

484
00:28:53,700 --> 00:28:55,110
Then why can't you share a room with him?

485
00:28:55,630 --> 00:28:57,140
Why should I do it, though?

486
00:28:57,790 --> 00:28:59,080
Because you should be able to!

487
00:28:59,310 --> 00:29:00,770
But why?

488
00:29:01,180 --> 00:29:03,290
Jeez, just share a room with him.

489
00:29:03,460 --> 00:29:05,810
This doesn't happen every day, you know.

490
00:29:09,920 --> 00:29:10,870
You're so nosy.

491
00:29:11,260 --> 00:29:12,620
Do you not want a boyfriend?

492
00:29:13,460 --> 00:29:14,590
None of your business.

493
00:29:14,620 --> 00:29:15,330
Hey!

494
00:29:16,490 --> 00:29:17,890
I'm just clearing the way for you.

495
00:29:27,910 --> 00:29:28,730
Tod!

496
00:29:31,970 --> 00:29:33,620
Your friends are so funny.

497
00:29:36,430 --> 00:29:39,110
Bumm said Tod and Art are so eccentric.

498
00:29:41,730 --> 00:29:42,700
What about me?

499
00:29:43,600 --> 00:29:44,460
Am I not funny?

500
00:29:45,560 --> 00:29:46,430
Let go of me.

501
00:29:52,130 --> 00:29:53,950
My friends love the sea.

502
00:29:55,050 --> 00:29:57,650
They always want to come here after exams.

503
00:30:00,020 --> 00:30:03,020
But the one who loved it most was probably Anda.

504
00:30:04,530 --> 00:30:05,920
He was even counting down the days.

505
00:30:28,280 --> 00:30:30,160
We were so happy back then.

506
00:30:31,560 --> 00:30:32,490
This should be ready.

507
00:30:32,510 --> 00:30:34,080
This one? Looks like it's almost ready.

508
00:30:36,160 --> 00:30:37,860
Is that everything? Let's go.

509
00:30:37,880 --> 00:30:39,760
- Even when Kum joined us...
- I'll bring it over.

510
00:30:40,020 --> 00:30:41,520
This semester has been exhausting.

511
00:30:41,550 --> 00:30:43,800
- Go help them grill the BBQ.
- Everything was still great.

512
00:30:44,180 --> 00:30:47,560
- Alright, cheers!
- Cheers! Whoa.

513
00:30:48,530 --> 00:30:49,740
Fruits, guys.

514
00:30:51,290 --> 00:30:53,720
- Thank you, Kum and Anda,
- Thank you so much.

515
00:30:53,750 --> 00:30:57,420
for this meal.

516
00:30:57,620 --> 00:31:01,350
Kum, why is this BBQ so sweet?

517
00:31:01,380 --> 00:31:04,590
Right, Tod? I don't think
they're supposed to add sugar to BBQ.

518
00:31:04,850 --> 00:31:06,390
Is it because the person grilling it is in love?

519
00:31:07,600 --> 00:31:08,450
Too bad...

520
00:31:10,650 --> 00:31:12,120
we didn't get to come together this year.

521
00:31:16,620 --> 00:31:17,920
Sometimes I wonder...

522
00:31:20,670 --> 00:31:22,640
what the hell I've gotten myself into.

523
00:31:25,410 --> 00:31:27,120
I don't even know how my friend died.

524
00:31:29,210 --> 00:31:30,820
Things are getting out of control.

525
00:31:35,160 --> 00:31:36,040
Jin...

526
00:31:45,340 --> 00:31:46,520
I'm right here.

527
00:31:48,690 --> 00:31:50,790
No matter what happens,
I'll be right here with you.

528
00:32:06,720 --> 00:32:08,430
No, I'm not riding on your back.

529
00:32:13,990 --> 00:32:14,820
Come on.

530
00:32:15,040 --> 00:32:15,940
There we go.

531
00:32:37,170 --> 00:32:38,400
What are you two doing?

532
00:32:40,930 --> 00:32:42,590
- Get in the sea.
- Wanna get in the sea?

533
00:32:42,850 --> 00:32:44,900
Wanna get in the sea?

534
00:32:46,580 --> 00:32:47,600
Podduang!

535
00:32:48,060 --> 00:32:49,980
One, two, three.

536
00:32:56,270 --> 00:32:58,660
Do you guys come to the same place every year?

537
00:32:59,420 --> 00:33:02,520
Of course. And Art gets drunk like this
every year, too.

538
00:33:04,460 --> 00:33:07,450
What's up, Art?
Does getting drunk make you feel down?

539
00:33:11,970 --> 00:33:13,250
I miss Anda.

540
00:33:17,090 --> 00:33:19,270
We come here together every year.

541
00:33:20,550 --> 00:33:22,610
Being here without him is just...

542
00:33:24,190 --> 00:33:25,620
Why did he have to die?

543
00:33:27,370 --> 00:33:29,840
Art, that's enough. Stop drinking, man.

544
00:33:31,690 --> 00:33:34,190
So what do you guys think...

545
00:33:34,420 --> 00:33:35,280
about this?

546
00:33:35,760 --> 00:33:36,890
Who do you think did it?

547
00:33:38,410 --> 00:33:40,290
I don't know who did it yet,

548
00:33:40,570 --> 00:33:43,330
but I've got tons of ideas
about how they did it.

549
00:33:44,650 --> 00:33:45,590
What do you mean?

550
00:33:45,940 --> 00:33:49,180
I mean, I want to know
how he was killed, too.

551
00:33:50,220 --> 00:33:52,120
The footage confirmed that...

552
00:33:52,240 --> 00:33:54,790
Anda drove there
and parked the car all by himself.

553
00:33:55,740 --> 00:33:58,660
Even though there's no footage after that,

554
00:33:59,220 --> 00:34:00,900
the timing fits with his death.

555
00:34:01,990 --> 00:34:04,200
What if the killer struck
while the car was parked?

556
00:34:04,500 --> 00:34:07,070
Why didn't Anda just open the door
and get out, right?

557
00:34:07,690 --> 00:34:10,850
Why would he just fall asleep and suffocate?

558
00:34:11,150 --> 00:34:13,310
Right? That's what's suspicious.

559
00:34:14,290 --> 00:34:15,219
Guess what?

560
00:34:15,850 --> 00:34:17,449
If you modify a car...

561
00:34:18,320 --> 00:34:20,000
by installing a control unit

562
00:34:20,710 --> 00:34:23,750
and connecting it to a phone
with just a little setup,

563
00:34:24,909 --> 00:34:26,800
it basically becomes a magic remote

564
00:34:26,920 --> 00:34:28,780
that lets you control the car.

565
00:34:29,389 --> 00:34:30,090
What?

566
00:34:30,520 --> 00:34:32,120
There's no way you could do that with a remote.

567
00:34:32,590 --> 00:34:33,600
It's really possible.

568
00:34:34,150 --> 00:34:37,540
If the car's control unit
gets hacked and re-paired,

569
00:34:38,159 --> 00:34:41,449
the car can be locked or unlocked
by someone outside.

570
00:34:42,330 --> 00:34:43,730
You've watched too many movies, Tod.

571
00:34:44,310 --> 00:34:45,880
Does that kind of remote really exist?

572
00:34:46,730 --> 00:34:47,639
Hey.

573
00:34:48,389 --> 00:34:50,139
It's just like a Bluetooth speaker.

574
00:34:50,530 --> 00:34:52,130
We're studying mechanical engineering.

575
00:34:52,460 --> 00:34:53,710
The professor even mentioned it.

576
00:34:54,780 --> 00:34:56,070
I've been thinking about it, too.

577
00:34:56,540 --> 00:34:58,010
This could be how he was killed.

578
00:35:00,040 --> 00:35:01,030
I think...

579
00:35:01,660 --> 00:35:04,050
the only way we're gonna get anywhere now

580
00:35:04,500 --> 00:35:07,590
is if we find Anda's laptop or phone.

581
00:35:08,740 --> 00:35:09,410
And...

582
00:35:10,440 --> 00:35:12,160
why are you so sure...

583
00:35:12,740 --> 00:35:14,160
that you'll find something in there?

584
00:35:15,560 --> 00:35:16,310
I don't know.

585
00:35:17,570 --> 00:35:18,940
I just know we have to find them.

586
00:35:36,270 --> 00:35:37,370
Where's the hair dryer?

587
00:35:39,020 --> 00:35:41,560
Oh, Bumm borrowed it this afternoon.

588
00:35:43,410 --> 00:35:44,690
She probably forgot to return it.

589
00:35:46,100 --> 00:35:46,740
Okay.

590
00:35:51,140 --> 00:35:51,990
Jeez.

591
00:35:53,300 --> 00:35:55,780
Are you a dog? You got it all over me.

592
00:35:57,170 --> 00:35:59,620
My hair is wet. What am I supposed to do?

593
00:36:01,100 --> 00:36:03,050
Go sit down. I'll dry it for you.

594
00:36:14,240 --> 00:36:15,110
Are you sleepy?

595
00:36:16,210 --> 00:36:19,260
Not yet. I need to let my food settle
since I ate so much.

596
00:36:20,310 --> 00:36:21,570
You ate so much?

597
00:36:22,060 --> 00:36:23,450
You barely ate anything.

598
00:36:23,920 --> 00:36:26,820
I ate just fine.
You're the one who ate a lot.

599
00:36:27,500 --> 00:36:30,560
Well, I'm an athlete.

600
00:36:30,820 --> 00:36:32,460
It's normal for me to eat a lot.

601
00:36:34,780 --> 00:36:35,520
Well,

602
00:36:36,350 --> 00:36:37,560
what do you like to eat?

603
00:36:38,280 --> 00:36:40,210
You always order fried rice.

604
00:36:41,440 --> 00:36:42,740
Railway fried rice.

605
00:36:44,730 --> 00:36:45,530
Really?

606
00:36:54,760 --> 00:36:55,710
That's such a cute name.

607
00:36:56,940 --> 00:36:58,070
Railway fried rice?

608
00:36:58,610 --> 00:36:59,560
What's so cute about it?

609
00:37:02,620 --> 00:37:05,610
I don't know. It just sounds cute.

610
00:37:06,700 --> 00:37:07,800
And...

611
00:37:08,590 --> 00:37:09,750
when is your birthday?

612
00:37:10,900 --> 00:37:11,870
Why are you asking?

613
00:37:13,120 --> 00:37:15,360
I just want to get to know you.

614
00:37:16,950 --> 00:37:18,230
I was born on Saturday, the fifth

615
00:37:18,910 --> 00:37:19,850
of the fifth month.

616
00:37:20,520 --> 00:37:23,330
Whoa, making it sound complicated, huh?

617
00:37:25,450 --> 00:37:27,390
What about you?
When's your birthday?

618
00:37:28,670 --> 00:37:29,380
I'm not telling you.

619
00:37:33,500 --> 00:37:34,950
You're younger than me, aren't you?

620
00:37:36,120 --> 00:37:37,380
That's why you're not telling me.

621
00:37:41,310 --> 00:37:43,050
Not telling you.

622
00:37:50,550 --> 00:37:51,440
Just tell me.

623
00:37:53,680 --> 00:37:56,050
Your future boyfriend
is going to buy you a gift.

624
00:38:08,360 --> 00:38:09,570
Do you not want a boyfriend?

625
00:38:10,480 --> 00:38:11,720
I'm just clearing the way for you.

626
00:39:02,620 --> 00:39:03,810
Can't sleep?

627
00:39:05,150 --> 00:39:06,030
Yeah.

628
00:39:08,810 --> 00:39:09,730
The blanket...

629
00:39:10,130 --> 00:39:11,880
If it's in the way,
you can throw it down here.

630
00:39:12,050 --> 00:39:13,340
The AC is blowing right on me.

631
00:39:18,560 --> 00:39:20,480
Really? Are you cold?

632
00:39:22,230 --> 00:39:23,550
It's not that cold,

633
00:39:24,620 --> 00:39:27,930
but you were tossing the blanket around
like you were annoyed.

634
00:39:29,870 --> 00:39:31,500
I wasn't annoyed.

635
00:39:31,750 --> 00:39:32,990
I just couldn't sleep.

636
00:39:39,010 --> 00:39:40,200
You...

637
00:39:40,970 --> 00:39:42,460
can sleep up here if you want.

638
00:39:48,350 --> 00:39:49,050
Well...

639
00:39:50,840 --> 00:39:52,830
the AC is blowing on you, isn't it?

640
00:40:12,330 --> 00:40:14,970
I know you're stressing over
what happened to Anda,

641
00:40:18,650 --> 00:40:19,870
but I promise...

642
00:40:21,300 --> 00:40:22,630
that no matter what happens,

643
00:40:24,270 --> 00:40:25,870
I'll always be here for you.

644
00:40:36,220 --> 00:40:37,080
Thanks.

645
00:41:44,420 --> 00:41:45,600
I'm not messing around this time.

646
00:41:47,920 --> 00:41:48,760
What?

647
00:41:50,490 --> 00:41:51,270
Get up.

648
00:45:38,740 --> 00:45:40,830
The congee is already mushy, man.

649
00:45:44,010 --> 00:45:45,440
My friend is even worse.

650
00:45:48,510 --> 00:45:49,500
Jin!

651
00:45:50,870 --> 00:45:51,840
Jin.

652
00:45:54,080 --> 00:45:55,100
Jin!

653
00:45:56,340 --> 00:45:57,340
That's mine.

654
00:45:58,810 --> 00:46:00,220
Yours is over there.

655
00:46:04,340 --> 00:46:07,840
I couldn't sleep a wink last night.
It was so freaking loud.

656
00:46:08,450 --> 00:46:09,550
No, it wasn't.

657
00:46:10,140 --> 00:46:11,160
What?

658
00:46:11,460 --> 00:46:14,100
Tod was snoring.
That's what I was trying to say.

659
00:46:14,950 --> 00:46:17,320
Jeez, before I fell asleep,

660
00:46:17,600 --> 00:46:20,480
I heard something that sounded like
a cow being slaughtered.

661
00:46:23,110 --> 00:46:25,250
What was it? Was something wrong?

662
00:46:25,810 --> 00:46:28,400
It's this guy.
He always sings when he's drunk.

663
00:46:28,540 --> 00:46:29,920
I can handle him singing,

664
00:46:30,640 --> 00:46:32,560
but when he sings out of tune,
I can't take it.

665
00:46:39,530 --> 00:46:41,780
So, how was it for you two?

666
00:46:44,610 --> 00:46:45,560
Everything was fine.

667
00:46:45,580 --> 00:46:46,990
I slept in my room,
and Jin slept on the couch.

668
00:46:47,270 --> 00:46:49,040
It was perfectly fine.

669
00:46:49,230 --> 00:46:52,620
I slept on the couch,
and Podduang slept in his room.

670
00:46:54,490 --> 00:46:55,880
Oh...

671
00:47:06,930 --> 00:47:08,670
Don't wanna date an engineering student?

672
00:47:09,330 --> 00:47:10,110
No.

673
00:47:11,030 --> 00:47:12,630
Then how about dating a soccer player?

674
00:47:13,620 --> 00:47:14,570
You know,

675
00:47:14,590 --> 00:47:16,570
Anda was always targeted by haters.

676
00:47:16,760 --> 00:47:18,910
There's this one account
that's been stirring up all the hate.

677
00:47:18,930 --> 00:47:20,580
It must be one of these five people.

678
00:47:20,700 --> 00:47:23,840
There's no way Anda
would've let himself suffocate in that car.

679
00:47:23,860 --> 00:47:26,480
Could it be that someone made him take pills?

680
00:47:26,540 --> 00:47:27,600
Or drugged him.

681
00:47:28,300 --> 00:47:29,400
Take a deep breath.

682
00:47:30,080 --> 00:47:31,600
I've figured out who killed Anda.

683
00:47:31,710 --> 00:47:33,000
If Anda was really murdered,

684
00:47:33,280 --> 00:47:34,230
then I...

685
00:47:35,090 --> 00:47:36,650
will bring the killer to justice myself.

